# Line endings.
#
# This repository is cloned on a Linux VM and its files are read by Linux tools,
# but it may pass through a Windows machine on the way. Git on Windows would
# otherwise check these out with CRLF endings, and a stray carriage return
# breaks things in ways that never mention line endings as the cause:
#
#   check-normalisation.sh  ->  bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M
#   a YAML manifest         ->  parse errors pointing at the wrong line
#
# Forcing LF in the working tree removes the whole class of problem.

*           text=auto eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
